<article class="env-lemma" id="04KV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04KV">Lemma <span data-tag="04KV">33.7.14</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ be a scheme over $k$. Assume $X$ is connected and has a point $x$ such that $k$ is algebraically closed in $\kappa (x)$. Then $X$ is geometrically connected. In particular, if $X$ has a $k$-rational point and $X$ is connected, then $X$ is geometrically connected. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Set $T = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\kappa (x))$. Let $\overline{k}$ be a separable algebraic closure of $k$. The assumption on $\kappa (x)/k$ implies that $T_{\overline{k}}$ is irreducible, see Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/037P" data-tag="037P">10.47.8</a>. Hence by Lemma <a href="/tag/056R" data-tag="056R">33.7.13</a> we see that $X_{\overline{k}}$ is connected. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0387" data-tag="0387">33.7.7</a> we conclude that $X$ is geometrically connected. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>